# New pillar, wave 3. Minimal shell wiring — NOT the wave 6 shell rewrite.
# app.tsx is already described by two legacy spec dirs (editor-shell and
# editor-inspector); neither is evolved here, per the co-evolution rule
# about historical pillars. This spec covers only what the canvas rewrite
# forces: constructing the two new stores and handing them down.
#
# Three things change and nothing else:
#   1. App owns UiState and Scene, built once per loaded document, and
#      passes them to Canvas (which no longer takes EditorState).
#   2. The theme stops being `create(ThemeSchema, {})`. That empty theme is
#      finding §5.7 — the editor renders with no styling at all and
#      disagrees with the CLI. It becomes the bundled blueprint theme,
#      which is the whole point of the themes-blueprint pillar (D12b).
#   3. A temporary bridge keeps the existing Inspector working.
#
# DELIBERATE TEMPORARY STATE, disclosed: SelectionContext and
# canvas/selection.ts survive this pillar. inspector.tsx consumes both
# (useSelection, and the numeric ElementKind enum), and migrating it to
# ElementRef belongs with the inspector v2 rewrite in wave 5 rather than
# being smuggled in here. So App keeps the provider and syncs UiState ->
# SelectionContext one-way with a small effect. Two selection stores exist
# for two waves; the canvas one is authoritative and the bridge is
# one-way, so they cannot disagree. The bridge and selection.ts both die
# in wave 5.

file: "packages/editor/src/shell/app.tsx"
doc: "Root shell: adapters, document state, and now the UiState + Scene stores."

constants: [
  { name: "App"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Additions to the existing component, which is otherwise unchanged:\n"
      "\n"
      "Theme: replace the empty `create(ThemeSchema, {})` with\n"
      "getBundledTheme('blueprint') from @archeglyph/themes. Add the\n"
      "workspace dependency to packages/editor/package.json if it is not\n"
      "already there. This is what makes the canvas and `archeglyph render`\n"
      "agree, and what makes the approved visual direction actually appear.\n"
      "\n"
      "Stores: one createUiState() for the session. A Scene built from the\n"
      "loaded EditorState via createScene(state, () => theme, layoutEngine),\n"
      "where layoutEngine is the browser one — LayoutEngineImpl over\n"
      "ElkAdapterImpl over createBrowserElk(), constructed once at module\n"
      "scope exactly as canvas.tsx does today, NOT per render. Both are\n"
      "created only once a document has loaded, since createScene needs a\n"
      "real EditorState.\n"
      "\n"
      "Canvas now receives scene, ui, diagram, stylesheet, theme and\n"
      "layoutEngine instead of state and theme.\n"
      "\n"
      "Bridge: a createEffect mirroring the first entry of\n"
      "ui.selection() into the existing SelectionState.setSelected, mapping\n"
      "the string kind to the numeric ElementKind the current Inspector\n"
      "expects, and null when the selection is empty. One-way only — the\n"
      "Inspector must never write back into UiState.\n"
      "\n"
      "Leave the load/open/keyboard-undo logic, the Resizable layout, and\n"
      "TopBar exactly as they are; they belong to other waves."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<{}>" } }
    uses: [
      "Canvas", "Scene", "UiState", "createScene", "createUiState",
      "getBundledTheme", "LayoutEngineImpl", "ElkAdapterImpl", "createBrowserElk"
    ]
  }
]
